    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d588">

                <pb facs="0566" n="476" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg476"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/1987</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Moscow</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Poole</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract]<anchor n="1" xml:id="d588-f1"
                        /></seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-05-29T15:00:00+02:31"><hi rendition="#italic">May 29, 1918, 3
                                p.m.</hi></date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received June 9, 10.21 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>576. … Halsey telegraphs from Murman May 25: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Notwithstanding orders received direct from Moscow Commissariat Foreign
                            Affairs, district Soviet desires Allies to remain. They <pb facs="0567"
                                n="477" xml:id="pg477"/> inform me in writing that their feelings
                            toward United States are most sincere and cordial and that this
                            friendship will only be cemented by presence American warship. <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Olympia</hi> arrived 24th and is under orders
                            British admiral.</p></quote></p>
                <p>Bolsheviks probably hope that by Murman cession to Finland they can avoid issue
                    through direct clash between Allies on one side and Finland and Germany on
                    other. …</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Poole</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
